{"Duplicate memory counting in submit() method causes incorrect backpressure decisions - when checking Redis memory usage, the code iterates through all buffers and calls get_memory_info() on each, which returns cluster-wide memory information. Since all buffers share the same Redis cluster, this causes the same memory to be counted multiple times (once per buffer/process), causing premature backpressure when max_memory_percentage is checked": 0.8643863201141357, "Dead code - unused _create_process_for_shard method is defined but never called anywhere in the codebase, appears to be leftover from refactoring when transitioning from per-shard processes to process-to-shards mapping": 0.30365678668022156}